Package: loglens
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/loglens/loglens
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libgl1, libegl1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3,
 libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcb-cursor0,
 libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0,
 libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xfixes0, libxcb-xkb1, libxcb-shm0, libxcb-sync1, libxcb-render0,
 libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0
Recommends: systemd, libnotify-bin, acl, polkitd | policykit-1
Suggests: docker.io | docker-ce
Description: see every service's logs and what they mean
 LogLens discovers the logs on a Linux machine (systemd services, Docker
 containers and Compose projects, and log files such as Squid, ClamAV and
 nginx), shows each service's logs live and separately, and explains in plain
 language what is happening, with probable causes and next steps.
 .
 Everything stays on the machine; secrets are removed before logs are stored;
 it never needs root. The optional loglens-helper service streams selected
 logs to authorized users without changing their groups.
 .
 This package bundles its own Python runtime and Qt under /opt/loglens.
